      "content": "I'm truly sorry to hear how you're feeling. It's understandable to feel numb or empty when faced with such a profound loss—it's a process that takes time. You might also consider writing a letter to express everything you wish you could say, or trying to create new rituals that bring comfort. It's okay to not have everything figured out yet, and it's okay to grieve. If it feels helpful, reaching out to a grief counselor might provide you with additional support and tools to navigate through these challenging emotions. Remember, moving on doesn't mean forgetting; it means finding a way to remember and allow yourself to love and grieve in your own time.",
